{"claims":[{"claim_text":"National DSA resources will be primarily devoted to building DSA through work for national and state-level Medicare for All.", "claim_types":["policy_position"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"The NPC and national staff, coordinating with a national DSA Medicare for All Working Group and other relevant national committees and working groups, will coordinate with chapters.", "claim_types":["policy_position"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"The NPC and national staff, coordinating with a national DSA Medicare for All Working Group and other relevant national committees and working groups, will intentionally develop and engage disabled comrades in the fight for Medicare for All.", "claim_types":["policy_position"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"A national single-payer working group will help chapters develop organizing strategies most relevant to their states and localities.", "claim_types":["policy_position"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"Defense of the existing single-payer parts of the health care system (Medicaid and Medicare) will be incorporated into DSA’s work, particularly in states that have rejected the expansion of Medicaid under the terms of the Affordable Care Act (Obamacare).", "claim_types":["policy_position"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"DSA will explore whether a national day of action would best strengthen both DSA’s single-payer work and the national movement for Medicare for All, taking into account financing, strength of coalition partners, and, in the case of a march, what city/cities should be targeted.", "claim_types":["policy_position"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"DSA will work with a speakers bureau to develop DSA member organizers (and possibly Canadian allies) who can speak effectively on why single-payer as well as socialized medicine is the best vision for healthcare, how a feasible Medicare for All would work and what strategy for winning the demand would be.", "claim_types":["policy_position"],"evidence_ids":[2]},{"claim_text":"Eliminating the profit motive in all levels of healthcare is necessary.", "claim_types":["policy_position"],"evidence_ids":[2]},{"claim_text":"DSA will work to empower locals to develop close relationships with allies in the national Medicare for All and state-level single-payer political blocs.", "claim_types":["policy_position"],"evidence_ids":[3]},{"claim_text":"The national Medicare for All and state-level single-payer political blocs are largely made up of women workers and, disproportionately, Black and Latino workers.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[3]},{"claim_text":"Working alongside the national Medicare for All and state-level single-payer political blocs will help expand DSA’s base among healthcare workers and nurses.", "claim_types":["prediction"],"evidence_ids":[3]},{"claim_text":"Working alongside the national Medicare for All and state-level single-payer political blocs will help expand DSA’s base among a broader more representative layer of the US working class.", "claim_types":["prediction"],"evidence_ids":[3]}],"unresolved_references":[]}
